-- EXPECT-ERROR: `Cap(IO.FileWrite)` used in module `IfaceSig` but `IO.FileWrite` is not declared in `needs`
-- R8 AUDIT — an INTERFACE method signature is a capability position (2026-08-06).
--
-- Found auditing the R8 runtime-escape-hatch table, and it is a gap left by
-- the R3 work rather than a pre-existing one. When Check 1's decl walk was
-- made exhaustive on 2026-08-05, `DInterface` and `DImpl` were enumerated
-- under "names no capability position". That was an explicit decision and it
-- was wrong: a method signature is a signature, and Check 1 treats every other
-- signature — plain `fn`, actor handler, `extern` — as a use.
--
-- The enumeration is why this is a visible mistake rather than a silent hole:
-- the arm names the constructors it skips, so the wrong call is reviewable in
-- the source instead of hiding behind `| _ -> []`. That is the whole argument
-- for banning the wildcard, and this file is the argument being cashed.
--
-- Nothing else in this module mentions a capability — no type declaration, no
-- `fn` signature, no body annotation — so only the interface can be what
-- fires. Accept companion: accept/t149.
mod IfaceSig do
  needs IO.Console

  interface Grantor(a) do
    fn grant : a -> Cap(IO.FileWrite)
  end

  fn main() do
    println("the only capability here is in an interface method signature")
  end
end
